      "sourceHash": "6ecc39cc95c7d919039a4f53e1aebb12144c489eb291147eaf65eefaea00e143",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.375,
          "end": 4.006,
          "en": "So to finalize this application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.006,
          "end": 7.95,
          "en": "it would be nice if we could also remove places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.95,
          "end": 10.492,
          "en": "from down there by clicking on them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.492,
          "end": 15.492,
          "en": "And for that, I got an endpoint in this dummy backend code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.729,
          "end": 19.991,
          "en": "We can send delete requests to this path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.991,
          "end": 23.742,
          "en": "to delete favorite places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.742,
          "end": 26.019,
          "en": "Now, what's special about this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.019,
          "end": 29.495,
          "en": "is that it actually doesn't take any request body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.495,
          "end": 34.245,
          "en": "but instead, it has a dynamic path parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.245,
          "end": 36.258,
          "en": "And this is, again, Node/Express code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.258,
          "end": 38.101,
          "en": "which you don't need to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.101,
          "end": 40.004,
          "en": "It has nothing to do with Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.004,
          "end": 45.004,
          "en": "but what it means is that we should incorporate the idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 50.228,
          "en": "of the place that should be deleted into the request path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.228,
          "end": 54.21,
          "en": "So after user-places/,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.21,
          "end": 57.663,
          "en": "we should have the idea of the place that should be deleted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.992,
          "end": 62.07,
          "en": "And that's, therefore, the kind of request we need to send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.07,
          "end": 62.903,
          "en": "from the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.903,
          "end": 67.903,
          "en": "Now, definitely feel free to implement this on your own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.92,
          "end": 71.368,
          "en": "with help of this removeUserPlace method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.368,
          "end": 73.788,
          "en": "Make sure that this method gets triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.788,
          "end": 77.22200000000001,
          "en": "whenever a user clicks one of these places down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.22200000000001,
          "end": 79.89,
          "en": "And make sure that a delete request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.89,
          "end": 82.896,
          "en": "is sent to that path I just explained",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.896,
          "end": 86.617,
          "en": "and that the ID is part of that path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.617,
          "end": 91.23400000000001,
          "en": "Also, consider handling errors if something goes wrong there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.23400000000001,
          "end": 96.232,
          "en": "and try implementing optimistic updating as we did it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.232,
          "end": 98.46000000000001,
          "en": "It's a nice exercise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.46000000000001,
          "end": 102.15,
          "en": "After a short pause, which you can use to pause the video,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.15,
          "end": 104.463,
          "en": "we'll implement this feature together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.50200000000001,
          "end": 111.856,
          "en": "So let's make these places removable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.856,
          "end": 115.5,
          "en": "For this to implement optimistic updating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.5,
          "end": 118.356,
          "en": "and to be able to roll it back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.356,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "I'll start by copying this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 126.52,
          "en": "from addPlaceToUserPlaces down to removeUserPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 128.129,
          "end": 132.737,
          "en": "And here, I now want to update my places array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 132.737,
          "end": 137.463,
          "en": "by removing the place which the user selected here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 138.358,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "For that, I first of all wanna check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 143.97,
          "en": "whether the selected place is part of my places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 143.97,
          "end": 147.746,
          "en": "so I'll perform the opposite check of what I had up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 147.746,
          "end": 152.746,
          "en": "I wanna check that the place is part of my previous places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 153.234,
          "end": 156.96,
          "en": "If that's the case, I wanna set my userPlaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 158.25,
          "en": "and I wanna set them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 158.25,
          "end": 163.25,
          "en": "to the result of calling prevPlaces.filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 164.485,
          "end": 167.256,
          "en": "where filter is another built-in method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 167.256,
          "end": 170.115,
          "en": "you can call on arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 170.115,
          "end": 172.62,
          "en": "Filter, like all of these functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 172.62,
          "end": 175.376,
          "en": "takes a function as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 175.376,
          "end": 179.742,
          "en": "which will be executed for every element in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 179.742,
          "end": 181.62,
          "en": "And that will then be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 181.62,
          "end": 183.876,
          "en": "as an argument to this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183.876,
          "end": 186.63,
          "en": "And we should then return true here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 186.63,
          "end": 189.27,
          "en": "if it's an element we wanna keep in the new array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.27,
          "end": 191.19,
          "en": "or false if it's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 191.19,
          "end": 192.738,
          "en": "And therefore, here, I wanna check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.738,
          "end": 195.75,
          "en": "if the ID of the place we're currently looking at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 195.75,
          "end": 198.42000000000002,
          "en": "in this array is not equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.42000000000002,
          "end": 201.43,
          "en": "to the idea of the place we selected for deletion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 203.7,
          "end": 206.64,
          "en": "because I wanna keep the place if the IDs are not equal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 208.879,
          "en": "If they are equal, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.879,
          "end": 211.252,
          "en": "it is the place I wanted to get rid of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.252,
          "end": 214.61,
          "en": "and therefore, filter should return false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.61,
          "end": 218.163,
          "en": "So that will update the userPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 219.362,
          "end": 222.494,
          "en": "Next, I wanna send a delete HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 222.494,
          "end": 227.494,
          "en": "And for this, I'll return this httpClient.delete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 227.994,
          "end": 231.367,
          "en": "And the URL to which the request should be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 231.367,
          "end": 236.367,
          "en": "is http:localhost:3000/user-places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 239.989,
          "end": 244.989,
          "en": "So this path and then slash and then the ID of the place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 247.2,
          "end": 252.2,
          "en": "So slash, and then I'll concatenate the place.id here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 252.486,
          "end": 255.123,
          "en": "to add it to the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 256.26,
          "end": 257.37,
          "en": "Now, just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 257.37,
          "end": 260.369,
          "en": "I'll then add the pipe method to add some operators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 260.369,
          "end": 264.346,
          "en": "or, specifically, here, one operator I wanna add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 264.346,
          "end": 267.03,
          "en": "I also want to catch errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 267.03,
          "end": 269.974,
          "en": "just as I did it when adding a place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 269.974,
          "end": 272.492,
          "en": "So I wanna catch any errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 272.492,
          "end": 277.49,
          "en": "And if an error occurs, I wanna reset my userPlaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 278.61,
          "end": 281.485,
          "en": "In addition, we can also use the errorService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 281.485,
          "end": 283.11,
          "en": "to show an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 283.11,
          "end": 288.11,
          "en": "and say, \"Failed to remove the selected place,\" for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 290.736,
          "end": 293.25,
          "en": "And also, say this down here, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 293.25,
          "end": 296.28,
          "en": "this message is actually never shown anywhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 296.28,
          "end": 297.483,
          "en": "but this is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 298.993,
          "end": 301.361,
          "en": "Well, and that's almost it, then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 301.361,
          "end": 304.368,
          "en": "At least, that's one way of implementing this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 304.368,
          "end": 307.73,
          "en": "We now just have to make sure that this method gets called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 307.73,
          "end": 310.473,
          "en": "if a user clicks on a place down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 311.989,
          "end": 315.861,
          "en": "And therefore, we have to go to the user-places.component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 315.861,
          "end": 319.228,
          "en": "to the template and add that listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 319.228,
          "end": 321.487,
          "en": "to the app-places component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 321.487,
          "end": 324.997,
          "en": "and listen to this selectPlace event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 324.997,
          "end": 328.978,
          "en": "and then call a onRemovePlace method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 328.978,
          "end": 331.503,
          "en": "or whatever you want to call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 331.503,
          "end": 334.253,
          "en": "And pass that dollar sign event variable to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 334.253,
          "end": 337.034,
          "en": "so that we get that emitted event data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 337.034,
          "end": 339.153,
          "en": "from the selectPlace event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 340.863,
          "end": 343.986,
          "en": "And in the userPlaces.component class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 343.986,
          "end": 347.997,
          "en": "maybe after ngOnInit, we can add this method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 347.997,
          "end": 352.366,
          "en": "Expect a place of type place as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 352.366,
          "end": 356.294,
          "en": "And in here, then use our placesService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 356.294,
          "end": 359.741,
          "en": "and call the removeUserPlace method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 359.741,
          "end": 362.763,
          "en": "and pass this place to this method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 364.53,
          "end": 368.553,
          "en": "Just as before, this actually will give us a subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 369.861,
          "end": 373.14300000000003,
          "en": "at least if we call subscribe here, which we should.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 374.01,
          "end": 376.413,
          "en": "And we should also clean up that subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 378.726,
          "end": 381.746,
          "en": "Now, we can then also add that observer object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 381.746,
          "end": 384.621,
          "en": "and listen to the next value or to errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 384.621,
          "end": 386.88,
          "en": "but if you're not planning to do anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 386.88,
          "end": 389.793,
          "en": "with that information, you don't need to do that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 391.26,
          "end": 393.513,
          "en": "So I'll just subscribe like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 394.73,
          "end": 396.986,
          "en": "Well, and that should be all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 396.986,
          "end": 400.627,
          "en": "If you now save that and you click on a place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 400.627,
          "end": 402.78,
          "en": "it should be removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 402.78,
          "end": 405.843,
          "en": "and if you reload, it should stay removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 406.735,
          "end": 411.19,
          "en": "And just to also check this as well, if you go to app.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 412.125,
          "end": 417.125,
          "en": "and there, you add an error to this delete route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 417.48199999999997,
          "end": 421.63,
          "en": "so if you send back a 500 response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 422.739,
          "end": 425.253,
          "en": "and you restart that backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 426.129,
          "end": 427.625,
          "en": "then you should actually see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 427.625,
          "end": 432.03,
          "en": "that if you try to delete one of these places down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 432.03,
          "end": 435.238,
          "en": "let's say the Sahara, it actually is readded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 435.238,
          "end": 439.26,
          "en": "and I got this modal, so I can't delete it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 439.26,
          "end": 442.738,
          "en": "which makes sense because that is the behavior we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 442.738,
          "end": 445.02,
          "en": "And with that, I'll get rid of this error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 445.02,
          "end": 446.229,
          "en": "and restart again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 446.229,
          "end": 450.03,
          "en": "so that we got the working application again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 450.03,
          "end": 453.75,
          "en": "If we now reload, deleting the Sahara down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 453.75,
          "end": 456.563,
          "en": "should be straightforward and should work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 456.563,
          "end": 460.53,
          "en": "And that's there, for now, the finished application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 460.53,
          "end": 462.731,
          "en": "where we have all these places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 462.731,
          "end": 467.731,
          "en": "and where we can add those places here without issues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 467.983,
          "end": 471.3,
          "en": "and where we can also remove those places if we want to.",
          "zh": ""
